SoupLite (Low-RAM Optimization Engine)
Author & Developer: Muhtar Jaksilikov

SoupLite is an independent low-RAM optimization framework developed by Muhtar Jaksilikov to enable LLM fine-tuning, post-training, dataset processing, and Web UI operations on low-resource machines with up to 2 GB RAM.

Inspiration & Acknowledgment:
The project architecture and concept were inspired by "Soup" (originally by Makazhan Alpamys). While original Soup requires a minimum of 4 GB+ RAM, SoupLite was completely re-architected and tuned by Muhtar Jaksilikov for strict sub-2 GB RAM execution limits.

